==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|deliteful}}, {{m|enm|delitfull}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|delight|ful|pos=adjective}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dəˈlaɪt.fəl/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-delightful.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{hyphenation|en|de|light|ful}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|more|er|delightfuller}}

# [[pleasant|Pleasant]]; [[pleasing#Adjective|pleasing]], bringing [[enjoyment]], [[satisfaction]], or [[pleasure]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1853|author={{w|Lewis Carroll}} {{quote-gloss|pseudonym; Charles Lutwidge Dodgson}}|chapter=The Two Brothers|editor=Stuart Dodgson Collingwood|title=The Lewis Carroll Picture Book{{nb...|A Selection from the Unpublished Writings and Drawings of Lewis Carroll, Together with Reprints from Scarce and Unacknowledged Work}}|location=London|publisher=[[w:T. Fisher Unwin|T{{quote-gloss|homas}} Fisher Unwin]]|year_published=1899|page=22|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/lewiscarrollpict00carruoft/page/22/mode/1up|oclc=2916259|passage=What? a higher delight to be drawn from the sight / Of fish full of life and of glee? / What a noodle you are! ’tis '''delightfuller''' far / To kill them than let them go free!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1888|author=Venier Voldo|chapter=Memoria in Eterna|title=Poems from the Pacific: The West’s Reply to England’s Laureate|edition=2nd|location=San Francisco, Calif.|publisher=[[w:Hubert Howe Bancroft|The Bancroft Company]]|page=134|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/poemsfrompacific00beerrich/page/n137/mode/1up|oclc=6589833|passage=O, Joy! quicker than fire! O, Hope of things! / O, gracious gladness mighty with delight! / O, subtle sweet, '''delightfuler''' than might! / Ah, me, no fiercer laughing unction springs / From the fair Hope of things!}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=6 July 1908|author=[[w:Samuel Langhorne Clemens|S{{quote-gloss|amuel}} L{{quote-gloss|anghorne}} Clemens]]|title=A Letter from Mark Twain: Innocence at Home|journal=[[w:Collier's|Collier’s]]|volume=XLI|issue=20|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Peter Fenelon Collier|P{{quote-gloss|eter}} F{{quote-gloss|enelon}} Collier & Son]]|year_published=8 August 1908|page=22|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_colliers-the-national-weekly_1908-08-08_41_20/page/n21/mode/1up|column=2|issn=2161-6469|oclc=8755061|passage=Hon. Collier Weekly which furnish Japanese Schoolboy to public not often enough, when is his book coming out? {{...}} That Boy is the dearest & sweetest & frankest & wisest & funniest & '''delightfulest''' & lovablest creation that has been added to our literature for a long time.|footer={{small|Transcription: {{cite-book|en|editors=Benjamin Griffin; Harriet Elinor Smith|year=2015|chapter=Explanatory Notes|title=w:Autobiography of Mark Twain|series=The Mark Twain Papers|volume=3|location=Berkeley, Calif.|publisher=w:University of California Press|page=599|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/autobiographyofm0003twai/page/599/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-520-27994-0}}.}}}}
#* {{RQ:Christie Autobiography|chapter=4|part=I|passage=An indulgent playmate, Grannie would lay aside the long scratchy-looking letter she was writing (heavily crossed 'to save notepaper') and enter into the '''delightful''' pastime of 'a chicken from Mr Whiteley's'.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2013/12/is-delightful-the-new-cool/282219/|title=Is ‘Delightful’ the New ‘Cool’?|date=2013-12-11|quotee=w:Marissa Mayer|author=Megan Garber|work=The Atlantic|passage=That is what I plan to do at Yahoo: give the end user something valuable and '''delightful''' that makes them want to come to Yahoo every day.}}

